{
    "title": "Remote Play Controller for PS",
    "description": "You can remote control and play much more easier with your smart Android devices. By streaming PS directly from your TV to your phone, you can enjoy remote gaming anywhere without the need for a TV. It only takes a few simple steps to connect your PS devices and log in to your PS account, allowing you to effortlessly remote play and control your PS4/PS5 with a single tap on your smartphone or tablet.\r\n\r\nThe Remote Controller for PS grants you complete access to control your PlayStation 5 console or PlayStation 4 console from a different location.\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\n- Use PS Remote Controller as virtual Dualshock controller for your Playstation 5/playstation4/PS4/PS5\r\n- Streaming from your Play Station4/PlayStation5/PS4/PS5 to your device with low latency\r\n- Control your PlayStation4 & PlayStation5/PS4/Ps5 by using the on-screen controller on your mobile device as your second screen for PS gameplay\r\n- 3rd Party, Dualsense/ Dualshock and physical controller support for all Android devices\r\n\r\nProceed with the instructions to utilize the Remote Play Controller for PS app:\r\n\u2022 You MUST configure your router at home to allow this\r\n\u2022 Log-in to An Account for PlayStation Network (PlayStation 4/ PlayStation 5/ PS4/ PS5)\r\n\u2022 A PlayStation 4/PS4 or PlayStation 5/PS5 console with the latest system software version\r\n\u2022 High-speed internet access (home Wi-Fi network)\r\n\u2022 Mobile device with Android 7.0 or later installed\r\n\u2022 You can register multiple PS4/ PS5/PlayStation 4/PlayStation 5 profiles\r\n\u2022 Remote Play Controller for PS supports rooted devices\r\n\u2022 Remote Play Controller for PS can be used as virtual Dualshock for your PS4/PS5/PlayStation4/PlayStation5.\r\n\r\nList of supported devices:\r\n\u2022 Supports Android TV devices\r\n\u2022 Supports older PS4 firmware from 5.05 and newer\r\n\u2022 A PS4/PS5/PlayStation4/PlayStation5 console with the latest system software version\r\n\r\nRemote Controller for PS is available under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3. The source is available at https://sites.google.com/view/license-ps",
    "descriptionHTML": "You can remote control and play much more easier with your smart Android devices. By streaming PS directly from your TV to your phone, you can enjoy remote gaming anywhere without the need for a TV. It only takes a few simple steps to connect your PS devices and log in to your PS account, allowing you to effortlessly remote play and control your PS4/PS5 with a single tap on your smartphone or tablet.<br><br>The Remote Controller for PS grants you complete access to control your PlayStation 5 console or PlayStation 4 console from a different location.<br><br>Features:<br>- Use PS Remote Controller as virtual Dualshock controller for your Playstation 5/playstation4/PS4/PS5<br>- Streaming from your Play Station4/PlayStation5/PS4/PS5 to your device with low latency<br>- Control your PlayStation4 &amp; PlayStation5/PS4/Ps5 by using the on-screen controller on your mobile device as your second screen for PS gameplay<br>- 3rd Party, Dualsense/ Dualshock and physical controller support for all Android devices<br><br>Proceed with the instructions to utilize the Remote Play Controller for PS app:<br>\u2022 You MUST configure your router at home to allow this<br>\u2022 Log-in to An Account for PlayStation Network (PlayStation 4/ PlayStation 5/ PS4/ PS5)<br>\u2022 A PlayStation 4/PS4 or PlayStation 5/PS5 console with the latest system software version<br>\u2022 High-speed internet access (home Wi-Fi network)<br>\u2022 Mobile device with Android 7.0 or later installed<br>\u2022 You can register multiple PS4/ PS5/PlayStation 4/PlayStation 5 profiles<br>\u2022 Remote Play Controller for PS supports rooted devices<br>\u2022 Remote Play Controller for PS can be used as virtual Dualshock for your PS4/PS5/PlayStation4/PlayStation5.<br><br>List of supported devices:<br>\u2022 Supports Android TV devices<br>\u2022 Supports older PS4 firmware from 5.05 and newer<br>\u2022 A PS4/PS5/PlayStation4/PlayStation5 console with the latest system software version<br><br>Re